.TH MD2EPUB 1 "November 2026" "mde 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
md2epub \- native Markdown to EPUB 2/3 e-book converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B md2epub
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIinput.md\fR [\fIoutput.epub\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B md2epub
is a native C11 command-line tool that converts CommonMark and extended Markdown
documents, along with linked local document graphs, into fully compliant EPUB 3 or
legacy EPUB 2.0.1 e-books.
.PP
Packaging is performed natively using \fBlibzip\fR, strictly enforcing the Open
Container Format (OCF) standard: the \fImimetype\fR file is stored uncompressed
(\fBZIP_CM_STORE\fR) at offset 0, followed by \fIMETA-INF/container.xml\fR,
\fIEPUB/package.opf\fR, navigation files, CSS stylesheets, bundled local images,
and valid XHTML 1.1 / HTML5 chapters.
.PP
By default, \fBmd2epub\fR automatically splits input documents into distinct
chapters at every H1 (\fB#\fR) heading and at linked Markdown document boundaries.
Internal cross-references and links between chapters are rewritten to valid intra-archive
anchors, and external URLs (e.g. \fIhttps://\fR) are fully preserved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIFILE\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Specify destination \fI.epub\fR archive path. Defaults to \fI<input_stem>.epub\fR.
.TP
.BR \-2 ", " \-\-epub2
Generate an EPUB 2.0.1 e-book with \fItoc.ncx\fR navigation map for older e-readers.
.TP
.BR \-3 ", " \-\-epub3
Generate a modern EPUB 3.2 e-book with semantic \fInav.xhtml\fR navigation document
(and backward-compatible NCX spine). This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fISTRING\fR ", " \-\-title " " \fISTRING\fR
Override the publication title (defaults to YAML front matter or the first H1 heading).
.TP
.BR \-a " " \fISTRING\fR ", " \-\-author " " \fISTRING\fR
Override the author / creator metadata.
.TP
.BR \-l " " \fICODE\fR ", " \-\-lang " " \fICODE\fR
Override the BCP 47 language code (defaults to \fIen\fR or YAML front matter).
.TP
.BR \-\-date " " \fISTRING\fR
Set the publication date (ISO 8601 or \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR format).
.TP
.BR \-\-publisher " " \fISTRING\fR
Set the publisher entity name.
.TP
.BR \-\-identifier " " \fISTRING\fR
Set a unique publication identifier (e.g., URN UUID or ISBN).
.TP
.BR \-\-rights " " \fISTRING\fR
Set the copyright or licensing statement.
.TP
.BR \-\-description " " \fISTRING\fR
Set the book description or abstract.
.TP
.BR \-\-cover " " \fIIMAGE_FILE\fR
Embed the specified image file (JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, or SVG) as the e-book cover,
creating a dedicated cover page and manifest cover metadata.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICSS_FILE\fR ", " \-\-css " " \fICSS_FILE\fR
Use a custom CSS stylesheet instead of the built-in typographic stylesheet.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-split
Do not split chapters on H1 headings; keep the entire input document in a single chapter.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-linked
Do not follow or bundle locally linked Markdown files (\fI[Link](chapter.md)\fR).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress progress reporting and informational output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and build information, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage instructions and options summary, then exit.
.SH YAML FRONT MATTER
\fBmd2epub\fR automatically detects and parses YAML front matter delimited by
\fB---\fR at the beginning of the Markdown file. Supported keys include:
.RS
.TP
.B title
Book title string.
.TP
.B author
Author name.
.TP
.B language
Language code (e.g., \fIen\fR, \fIsv\fR, \fIde\fR).
.TP
.B date
Publication date.
.TP
.B publisher
Publisher name.
.TP
.B identifier
Unique ID (UUID or ISBN).
.TP
.B rights
Copyright or licensing text.
.TP
.B description
Abstract or summary.
.TP
.B cover
Relative or absolute path to cover image.
.TP
.B css
Relative or absolute path to custom stylesheet.
.RE
.PP
Front-matter blocks are cleanly stripped from the generated chapter bodies. CLI flags
always take precedence over YAML front-matter values.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert a single Markdown file to an EPUB 3 e-book:
.B md2epub novel.md
.TP
Convert with custom title, author, and output path:
.B md2epub \-o /tmp/manual.epub \-\-title "User Manual" \-\-author "Tech Corp" guide.md
.TP
Generate an EPUB 2 e-book with custom CSS and a cover image:
.B md2epub \-2 \-\-cover cover.jpg \-c book.css thesis.md
